{
  "name": "Giant Raven (Druid Giant Raven mod): the Druid's Raven scaled up as a shapeshift form",
  "notes": [
    "Uniform scale 4.0: the reshaped body without its wings then covers about as much screen as the Werebear (equal silhouette area at a 30-degree camera, averaged over 8 directions: 1.70 sq model ft against 27.7 sq ft gives 4.03; the stock body needed 4.45). Wingspan about 26 ft.",
    "The stock clips fly far too high for a player form (neutral pelvis at 13.5 model ft, about 54 ft after scaling). Every clip here is lowered with a move on pelvis_bind_jnt: neutral-based clips by -10.6 (pelvis at 2.9 model ft = 11.6 ft in game: the reshaped wings' deepest downstroke, 2.87 below the pelvis, just clears the floor), walk-based ones by -6.53 (pelvis 3.15, downstroke 3.16). hover / fly / fall replace neutral / walk / death on NU / WL / DT, peck is the default A1; the stock clips stay in the file.",
    "Skeleton (druidhawk): +Y up, +Z forward, +X the bird's left. Wings: collar > shoulder > elbow > hand > finger > middle_base > middle > middle1 (tip), along +-X in the bind pose. Rotations about model axes: +X pitches nose/legs down-back (legs forward = negative), left wing up = +Z, right wing up = -Z, left wing back = +Y, right wing back = -Y. jaw_bind_jnt is the lower beak: +X opens it.",
    "Static base (\"at\": 0): the neutral clip's first pose (the glide pose, wings spread) held for the clip's duration at 60 keys per second, so the edits carry the whole motion and the clip starts and ends in that pose.",
    "Player modes (timing token now the Werewolf's, 40): charge (loop), block, spin (loop, an even 360-degree turn with \"ease\": \"linear\"), throw, leap_windup (ends crouched), leap_air (loop), leap_land and leap_strike (start in leap_air's pose), channel (loop). Loops use waves with \"fade\": false and whole cycles, so their ends meet.",
    "Own mesh: \"reshape\" (bind-pose model ft; bulk = scale about a pivot by bone share; shape = the same, or an offset, graded along an axis): heavier chest (spine3/4 + collars), belly, head x1.25 about the neck, thick lower beak, deeper upper beak with a hooked tip, a throat ruff pushed down and forward, longer primaries and secondaries, a wedge tail longer in the middle, bigger feet and talons, thicker shanks. retexture: the feather albedo recoloured block by block (darker, faint blue-violet) at a path of the same length, which the rewritten models point at. modelIndexIncludes: QuillRatDruid's models are carried in this mod's model index (install this mod after it)."
  ],
  "modelIndexIncludes": ["../QuillRatDruid"],
